   "html_text": "The short pamphlet’s appearance was a watershed in numerous respects. Scholastic cosmology held that, whereas the terrestrial elemental world with its diversity of natures exhibited multitudinous change, the aethereal heavens at most placidly and eternally rotated in their places. But Galileo’s telescope revealed a very Earth-like Moon, with mountains and valleys, and showed that Jupiter has moons just like the Earth’s. In both cases, the observations drew similarities between celestial objects ",
